## Summary

Tool-result sanitization is not enforced as a total sink-boundary invariant on current `main`. A tool result containing a credential-shaped value can be copied into one or more durable, logged, display, trajectory, or callback representations before a final non-reusable projection is applied.

Verified sink classes:

- spillover persistence and verbose tool-result logging;
- display and preview projections;
- session JSON snapshots emitted from session persistence;
- trajectory JSONL...
